<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<bpmn:definitions xmlns:bpmn="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL"
                  xmlns:bpmndi="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/DI"
                  xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DC"
                  xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DI"
                  xmlns:folio="https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/bpmn"
                  id="Definitions_BoardPlaceNote"
                  targetNamespace="http://folio-assistant.dev/bpmn/board-place-note">

  <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
       Placing a note on a board — folio-assistant
       Bean: folio-assistant-sd8x (authoring), folio-assistant-1rta (build)

       Owner, 2026-09-21: "create new stickt notes (this is tile) this
       dymanic moving state is overlayed, its an \"extra\". on stndard
       folio just simple tile based listing", and, on the arrows:
       "notes exist lower down than folio. make sure arrows correct."

       THE POINT OF DRAWING THIS is that creating a sticky and placing
       one are TWO WRITES TO TWO GRAPHS, and the common bug is to make
       them one. The note goes into the folio and carries no coordinate;
       the coordinate goes into `board-positions.json`, keyed by board
       and then by note. A reader who drags an existing card takes only
       the second path, which is why the gateway exists at all.

       ADVISORY, like `board-open-close`. Dragging a card is a gesture,
       not a gate; what must not drift is WHICH GRAPH each write lands
       in, and that is asserted in `board-positions.test.ts` against the
       source rather than gated here.
       ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->

  <bpmn:collaboration id="Collab_BoardPlaceNote">
    <bpmn:participant id="Participant_BoardPlaceNote" name="Board: place a note" processRef="Process_BoardPlaceNote"/>
  </bpmn:collaboration>

  <bpmn:process id="Process_BoardPlaceNote" name="Board: place a note" isExecutable="true">
    <bpmn:documentation>Putting a note at a spot on a board: write the note into the folio, record where it was drawn on THIS board, and sweep any position whose note has gone.

You are in this process whenever a note is to appear somewhere. The first gateway exists because the note may already be there — placing is not the same as creating, and a process that conflated them would duplicate content every time somebody moved something.

The rule the diagram holds is in the first activity's own wording: the note goes into the folio WITH NO COORDINATE. A folio is complete with no board, so a coordinate on a note would make the content depend on a drawing of it. The x,y belongs to the layer, keyed to one board, and an orphaned position is swept from the LAYER rather than being allowed to keep a note alive.</bpmn:documentation>
    <bpmn:extensionElements>
      <folio:policy enforcement="advisory"/>
    </bpmn:extensionElements>

    <bpmn:laneSet id="LaneSet_BoardPlaceNote">
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_Author" name="Author">
        <bpmn:documentation>Reached only on the `new sticky` branch of GW_Exists — dragging an existing card never re-enters this lane, because A_CreateNote is the one write to the folio and everything after it is positioning. Leaving out `x`, `y` and `board` here is what lets one note sit on several boards without this lane arbitrating between them; arbitration would make placement an authoring decision, which it is not.</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:extensionElements><folio:role ref="author"/></bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Start_Place</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>GW_Exists</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>A_CreateNote</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
      <!-- The layout layer. It is written every time and read by nothing
           that decides anything — losing it loses where, never what. -->
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_Layer" name="Layout layer">
        <bpmn:documentation>Every placement writes here, and nothing that decides anything reads it back — losing this graph loses WHERE a note sits, never WHAT it says. That asymmetry is why A_SweepOrphans cleans stray positions from this lane's own file rather than touching the note itself: the easy direction is removing a position whose note is gone, never removing a note because its position is.</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:extensionElements><folio:role ref="corpus"/></bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>A_Place</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>A_SweepOrphans</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>End_Placed</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
    </bpmn:laneSet>

    <bpmn:startEvent id="Start_Place" name="A note is to appear at a spot">
      <bpmn:outgoing>F_1</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:startEvent>

    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="GW_Exists" name="Does the note exist already?">
      <bpmn:incoming>F_1</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>F_New</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>F_Existing</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>

    <bpmn:task id="A_CreateNote" name="Write the note into the folio — with no coordinate">
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <!-- No `x`, no `y`, no `board`, no `position`, for the same reason
             a BPMN task carries none. One note may then sit on several
             boards at once without arbitrating between them. -->
        <folio:skill ref="board-diagram-interchange"/>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>F_New</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>F_Created</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>

    <bpmn:task id="A_Place" name="Record x,y for this note on THIS board">
      <bpmn:extensionElements><folio:skill ref="board-diagram-interchange"/></bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>F_Created</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>F_Existing</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>F_2</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>

    <bpmn:task id="A_SweepOrphans" name="Sweep positions whose note is gone">
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <!-- Swept from the LAYER, which is the easy direction: one file,
             one pass, and nothing edited out of a note a person owns. -->
        <folio:skill ref="board-diagram-interchange"/>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>F_2</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>F_3</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>

    <bpmn:endEvent id="End_Placed" name="The board shows it there">
      <bpmn:incoming>F_3</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>

    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F_1" sourceRef="Start_Place" targetRef="GW_Exists"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F_New" name="new sticky" sourceRef="GW_Exists" targetRef="A_CreateNote"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F_Existing" name="an existing card, dragged" sourceRef="GW_Exists" targetRef="A_Place"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F_Created" sourceRef="A_CreateNote" targetRef="A_Place"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F_2" sourceRef="A_Place" targetRef="A_SweepOrphans"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="F_3" sourceRef="A_SweepOrphans" targetRef="End_Placed"/>
  </bpmn:process>

  <!-- Layout only. Nothing below changes what the process does. -->
  <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="BPMNDiagram_BoardPlaceNote">
    <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="BPMNPlane_BoardPlaceNote" bpmnElement="Collab_BoardPlaceNote">
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Participant_BoardPlaceNote" bpmnElement="Participant_BoardPlaceNote" isHorizontal="true">
        <dc:Bounds x="160" y="80" width="920" height="400"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Lane_Author" bpmnElement="Lane_Author" isHorizontal="true">
        <dc:Bounds x="190" y="80" width="890" height="200"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Lane_Layer" bpmnElement="Lane_Layer" isHorizontal="true">
        <dc:Bounds x="190" y="280" width="890" height="200"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>

      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_Start_Place" bpmnElement="Start_Place">
        <dc:Bounds x="220" y="162" width="36" height="36"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_GW_Exists" bpmnElement="GW_Exists" isMarkerVisible="true">
        <dc:Bounds x="320" y="155" width="50" height="50"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_A_CreateNote" bpmnElement="A_CreateNote">
        <dc:Bounds x="430" y="140" width="140" height="80"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_A_Place" bpmnElement="A_Place">
        <dc:Bounds x="620" y="340" width="140" height="80"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_A_SweepOrphans" bpmnElement="A_SweepOrphans">
        <dc:Bounds x="820" y="340" width="140" height="80"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Shape_End_Placed" bpmnElement="End_Placed">
        <dc:Bounds x="1000" y="362" width="36" height="36"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>

      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Edge_F_1" bpmnElement="F_1">
        <di:waypoint x="256" y="180"/>
        <di:waypoint x="320" y="180"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Edge_F_New" bpmnElement="F_New">
        <di:waypoint x="370" y="180"/>
        <di:waypoint x="430" y="180"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Edge_F_Existing" bpmnElement="F_Existing">
        <di:waypoint x="345" y="205"/>
        <di:waypoint x="345" y="380"/>
        <di:waypoint x="620" y="380"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Edge_F_Created" bpmnElement="F_Created">
        <di:waypoint x="570" y="180"/>
        <di:waypoint x="690" y="180"/>
        <di:waypoint x="690" y="340"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Edge_F_2" bpmnElement="F_2">
        <di:waypoint x="760" y="380"/>
        <di:waypoint x="820" y="380"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Edge_F_3" bpmnElement="F_3">
        <di:waypoint x="960" y="380"/>
        <di:waypoint x="1000" y="380"/>
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
    </bpmndi:BPMNPlane>
  </bpmndi:BPMNDiagram>
</bpmn:definitions>
